<%# Navbar partial — rendered in application layout and admin navbar review.
    Locals (all optional):
      show_logged_in — override for logged_in? (default: real session)
      preview        — if true, disables scroll handler and sticky positioning
%>
<% show_user = local_assigns.fetch(:show_logged_in, logged_in?) %>
<% is_preview = local_assigns.fetch(:preview, false) %>

<%# --z-nav sits BELOW --z-modal. A modal is the active task, so its backdrop and
    card cover all persistent navigation chrome instead of appearing cut off
    beneath the navbar. Both tiers, and everything else that can block, come from
    the shared layer scale, which studio-engine owns OUTRIGHT — engine.css
    defines them and this app reads them through the engine build application.css
    imports. There is no local copy; the mirror that used to sit in
    application.css was deleted in delete-turf-layer-shim, because it outranked
    the gem it was mirroring. Toasts (--z-toast) and the environment bars
    (--z-banner) are the two layers deliberately above a modal. %>

<%# Toasts need nothing declared here or in application.css. The engine's own
    flash partial defaults its two override seams (--studio-toast-z and
    --studio-toast-blur-z) to the shared toast tiers, so the stack already
    clears the navbar and any open modal. This app set both from inside the old
    adoption shim, back when the engine defaulted them to a bare 60 and a toast
    fired from an open modal was invisible behind it. To move the toast layer,
    change the tier in studio-engine. %>
<%# vt-pinned-header (engine 0.24 smooth-load): names this header as the shared
    view-transition element so it stays pinned while page content cross-fades.
    NON-PREVIEW ONLY — the admin navbar-review page renders preview copies of
    this partial inside the body, and a duplicate view-transition-name silently
    disables ALL view transitions on the page. Exactly one pinned header per page. %>
<%# nav-shell is the --nav-p scope: navCollapse() writes the collapse progress
    (0 expanded .. 1 collapsed) on THIS element once per animation frame, and
    application.css derives the row padding, logo size, title size, balance size
    and username size from it with calc(). Nothing on the collapse path carries a
    time-based transition any more — see the factory's comment for the numbers
    that bought that. transition-shadow stays: box-shadow paints, it never
    reflows, so it cannot move content under the reader.
    Preview keeps nav-shell (the vars have to resolve) but no x-data — the
    /admin/navbar page drives --nav-p from its own Scrolled toggle. %>
<%# THE BARS ARE A SIBLING OF THE HEADER, ABOVE IT — not a child of it. They used
    to render inside <header>, and that is why the modal backdrop dimmed DEV MODE
    on QA: this header is `sticky` with a z-index, which makes it a STACKING
    CONTEXT, and a descendant's z-index is clamped inside its context. No value on
    the banner could escape a header composited at --z-nav. Outside it, the
    engine's `body.modal-open .studio-bar-stack` rule can lift them over the modal.

    Normal flow, no pin — the engine's bar_stack_test contracts exactly this shape
    (stack precedes header in document order, carries no positioning and no z-
    class of its own), so the bars keep scrolling up BEHIND the pinned header.
    Anything that needs to clear both reads --nav-bottom, which already reports
    the header's live bottom edge with chrome stacked above it. %>
<% unless is_preview %>
  <div class="studio-bar-stack w-full" data-studio-bar-stack>
    <%= render "studio/banners/environment", devnet: Solana::Config.devnet? %>
  </div>
<% end %>
<header data-navbar-root <%= 'x-data="navCollapse()"'.html_safe unless is_preview %>
        class="nav-shell <%= is_preview ? 'bg-page' : 'vt-pinned-header sticky top-0 z-[var(--z-nav)] bg-page transition-shadow duration-300' %>"
        <%= ":class=\"scrolled && 'shadow-lg border-b border-subtle is-scrolled'\"".html_safe unless is_preview %>>
  <%# THE IMPERSONATION BAR STAYS HERE, INSIDE THE PINNED HEADER, and the
      environment bar does not. They look alike and are not the same kind of
      thing:

        · The environment bar is an AMBIENT LABEL. "QA Environment · DEV MODE" is
          information, and the engine's banners/_stack records scrolling away as
          a deliberate, accepted trade for it. Moving it to the sibling stack is
          what buys it the modal-open lift.
        · The impersonation bar is an OPSEC CONTROL (OPSEC-046). It carries the
          escape hatch — a deliberately JS-free button_to "Return to <admin>"
          that works even if Alpine and Turbo never load — and an admin who
          scrolls must not lose either the warning or the way out. In the header
          it is pinned by construction, with no second sticky sibling to measure
          against.

      That is why only ONE of the two moved. The cost, stated rather than
      hidden: the impersonation bar is inside a header that carries a z-index and
      is therefore a stacking context, so it does NOT rise over an open modal the
      way the environment bar now does. Being permanently on screen is the
      property that matters for an escape hatch; being reachable through a modal
      is the property that matters for a QA toggle. Each one keeps its own.

      The environment bar moved OUT of this element to the sibling stack above —
      see the note there for why a stacking context made its z-index unreachable. The engine partial is still self-gating
      (studio-engine >= 0.30) and was built by lifting THIS app's behavior: the QA
      message composition, the DEVNET chip when devnet && !qa, and the
      link-vs-inert-chip email button. `preview:` is no longer forwarded because
      the whole stack is skipped in a preview render, which is what kept the
      /admin/navbar review page from painting a second banner — a duplicate
      pinned-header view-transition name silently disables every view transition
      on the page (smooth_load_component_test counts that class name here, so
      don't spell it again in prose). %>
  <%# .user-nav-col / .nav-title / .nav-logo / .nav-logo-link responsive
      rules live in app/assets/tailwind/application.css @layer utilities (migrated
      2026-05-24, dropped the 10 !important workarounds). %>
  <%= render "shared/impersonation_banner" if !is_preview && impersonating? %>
  <div class="nav-row flex items-center min-w-0">
    <%# Left side: logo + nav %>
    <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 px-4">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 min-w-0">
        <%= link_to root_path, class: "nav-logo-link inline-flex items-center gap-3 group" do %>
          <%# No w-*/h-* utility here: .nav-shell .nav-logo sizes it off --nav-p.
              transition-transform, NOT transition-all — the hover lift still
              eases, while width/height follow the finger with no clock. %>
          <img src="/icon-192.png" alt="Turf Totals" width="48" height="48" class="nav-logo rounded-full shadow-lg <%= "group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-300" unless is_preview %>">
          <h1 class="nav-title font-extrabold text-heading tracking-tight"><span class="dm-salmon">Turf</span><span class="dm-yellow text-primary">Totals</span></h1>
        <% end %>
        <nav class="dm-teal hidden md:flex items-center gap-4 min-w-0">
          <%= link_to "Contests", contests_path, class: "text-secondary hover:text-primary text-sm font-medium transition" %>
          <%= link_to "NFL Totals", nfl_team_totals_path, class: "text-secondary hover:text-primary text-sm font-medium transition" %>
          <%= link_to "Rules", turf_totals_v1_path, class: "text-secondary hover:text-primary text-sm font-medium transition" %>
          <%= link_to "Reserves", proof_of_reserves_path, class: "text-secondary hover:text-primary text-sm font-medium transition" %>
          <%= render "components/geo_badge" %>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>
    <%# Right side: user nav (matches sidebar width) %>
    <% balance_html = capture do %>
      <%# The balance SLOT holds two mutually exclusive faces:
            [data-balance-display]     the "$1284" wallet link
            [data-free-entry-label]    the "✨ Free Entry" stand-in
          A $0 balance held by a user WITH an entry token reads "✨ Free Entry"
          instead of a redundant "$0" — the amount they can enter for is zero
          dollars, which is the point, not an empty wallet. The same rule
          re-applies live through applyBalanceSlotRule() in solana_utils.js
          after mints + consumes, so server render and client never drift.
          The label ALSO peeks over the amount while the ✨ badge beside the
          avatar is hovered (.fe-peek, driven by freeEntryHover in _user_nav) —
          that is the answer to "what is this sparkle?". %>
      <%# display_balance is nil while the navbar cache is cold ("loading") —
          the server no longer blocks the render on the balance RPC. HIDE the
          whole balance link (incl. the "$") while loading so there's no lone
          "$" placeholder; client-side refreshBalance() then sets
          [data-balance-display] AND removes .hidden (its else-branch), so the
          full "$112" appears all at once. %>
      <% balance_loading = display_balance.nil? %>
      <% balance_dollars = display_balance.to_f %>
      <% balance_zero    = !balance_loading && balance_dollars.zero? %>
      <%# Cache-first (display_entry_token_count) — nil while cold counts as
          "no tokens" so we don't swap a real $0 balance during loading;
          applyBalanceSlotRule re-applies the swap after hydrate. %>
      <% has_tokens      = display_entry_token_count.to_i.positive? %>
      <% free_entry      = balance_zero && has_tokens %>
      <% hide_balance    = balance_loading || free_entry %>
      <div class="relative flex-shrink-0 leading-none mr-1"
           data-balance-slot="true"
           x-bind:class="freeEntryHover ? 'fe-peek' : ''">
        <%# nav-balance takes its font-size from --nav-p (xl -> lg) instead of a
            reactive class swap, which kept the size on Alpine's per-scroll path
            for a 2px change. transition-colors keeps the hover fade. %>
        <%= link_to wallet_path, class: "nav-balance dm-blue block font-mono text-primary hover:text-primary-600 transition-colors duration-300 font-bold leading-none #{'hidden' if hide_balance}", data: { balance_display: true } do %><% unless balance_loading %>$<%= balance_dollars.to_i %><% end %><% end %>
        <%# No size binding here: the two faces want DIFFERENT sizes (the peek is
            a compact pill, the stand-in matches the amount it replaces), so
            .free-entry-label / .is-active own font-size in application.css. %>
        <%= link_to wallet_path, class: "free-entry-label dm-blue gap-1 font-bold text-primary hover:text-primary-600 leading-none whitespace-nowrap #{'is-active' if free_entry}", data: { free_entry_label: true } do %><span class="fe-spark" aria-hidden="true">✨</span><span>Free Entry</span><% end %>
      </div>
    <% end if show_user %>
    <div class="user-nav-col dm-purple flex-shrink-0 min-w-0 pl-0 pr-4 md:px-4">
      <% if show_user %>
        <%= render "components/user_nav", balance_html: balance_html %>
      <% else %>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-end gap-3">
          <span class="hidden md:flex"><%= render "components/theme_toggle_morph" %></span>
          <%# Single unified CTA — login + signup are one create-or-login flow
              (magic link / Google / wallet all find-or-create). Opens the in-page
              auth modal at the credentials step; href=/signin is the no-JS
              fallback (the page still exists, just unrouted from here for now). %>
          <%= link_to "Sign in", signin_path, class: "btn btn-primary",
                "@click.prevent": "$store.modals.open('auth', { step: 'credentials', mode: 'signup', submitting: null, formError: '', phantomError: '', googleError: '' })" %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
  <%# Mobile sub-navbar: compact row of links hidden on desktop %>
  <div class="dm-coral flex md:hidden items-center gap-3 px-4 py-1.5 border-t border-subtle bg-surface-alt">
    <%= link_to "Contests", contests_path, class: "text-secondary hover:text-primary text-xs font-medium transition whitespace-nowrap" %>
    <%= link_to "NFL Totals", nfl_team_totals_path, class: "text-secondary hover:text-primary text-xs font-medium transition whitespace-nowrap" %>
    <%= link_to "Rules", turf_totals_v1_path, class: "text-secondary hover:text-primary text-xs font-medium transition whitespace-nowrap" %>
    <%= link_to "Reserves", proof_of_reserves_path, class: "text-secondary hover:text-primary text-xs font-medium transition whitespace-nowrap" %>
    <%= render "components/geo_badge" %>
    <span class="ml-auto flex items-center gap-3">
      <%= render "components/gear_sidebar_trigger" %>
      <%= render "components/theme_toggle_morph" %>
    </span>
  </div>
</header>
<%# --nav-h + overflow-anchor are shipped by studio-engine (>=0.4.4) from
    layouts/studio/_head.html.erb — no per-app navbar script needed. %>
